cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this library, please cite it as below.  The theory it
  mechanizes is due to Lanese, Phillips and Ulidowski; please cite their
  paper as well (see the references in README.md).
title: >-
  cslib-reversible: An axiom layer for reversible computation on top of
  CSLib's labelled transition systems
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the Lanese-Phillips-Ulidowski axioms for
  reversible computation (Square Property, Backward Transitions are
  Independent, well-foundedness) over CSLib's labelled transition systems,
  together with the theorems they entail: the Parabolic Lemma, causal
  consistency, causal safety and causal liveness.  A reversible language
  discharges the axioms once and inherits the theory.  The development is
  free of sorry and of Classical.choice.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tetsuo
    family-names: Yokoyama
    affiliation: Nanzan University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7677-143X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yokoyama-lab/cslib-reversible"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - reversible computation
  - labelled transition systems
  - causal consistency
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
